  "wiring": "workspace Cargo.toml: exclude = [\"vendor/libsqlite3-sys-0.28.0\"]; [patch.crates-io] libsqlite3-sys = { path = \"vendor/libsqlite3-sys-0.28.0\" }",
  "status": "Modified fork of upstream libsqlite3-sys 0.28.0. Three upstream files are patched (Cargo.toml, build.rs, sqlite3/sqlite3.c) and three RyeOS files are added (ryeos_instrument.rs, sqlite3/ryeos_binding.c, sqlite3/ryeos_binding.h), consumed by build.rs. The earlier 'exact upstream source extraction' claim was inaccurate for this tree and is withdrawn. files_sha256 records the actual bytes as of 2026-10-12. The RyeOS delta includes a compiled commit gate in vdbeCommit that calls the installed native verifier before every write-transaction commit, refusal of sqlite3_backup_init while the native arena exists, unconditional refusal of journal_mode=OFF in the bound-VFS build, opcode refusal while the verifier runs, and SQLITE_MAX_ATTACHED=0 (no ATTACH, VACUUM or VACUUM INTO). The tree is compiled by build.rs into every lillux-sqlite consumer and exercised by the lillux-sqlite tests and the daemon; the RyeOS delta has had targeted review of the native allocator and bound VFS but no complete independent audit against upstream."
